avformat/hls: drop WebVTT cues repeated across segment boundaries

Backport of FFmpeg commit ef53ec02d8 by Kacper Michajłow, as committed
upstream; the tests it adds are left out.

A WebVTT segment contains every cue shown during its period (RFC 8216,
3.5), so a cue that reaches into the next segment appears in both. Keep
the cues of the previous segment and drop the ones the current segment
repeats, so each cue is delivered once. The kept cues read before the
media position was known move onto it once it is, so the comparison is on
one timeline. Nothing is repeated across a discontinuity, so the kept cues
are dropped when the opened segment has another discontinuity sequence
number (RFC 8216, 4.3.3.3), which also covers a boundary that already left
a live playlist.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
